# Line endings.
#
# This repository is developed on Windows and its images are Linux. A CRLF that
# reaches a container is not a cosmetic problem: a shell script with CRLF fails
# with `no such file or directory` on its own shebang, and a Dockerfile heredoc
# or an entrypoint behaves the same way. So every file a Linux container reads is
# pinned to LF here, whatever the contributor's core.autocrlf is set to.
#
# The PowerShell scripts are deliberately left to Windows defaults: they run on
# the host, never in a container.

# Default: let Git decide for text, but never guess for the files below.
* text=auto

# --- files a Linux container reads or executes ---
*.sh            text eol=lf
Dockerfile      text eol=lf
Dockerfile.*    text eol=lf
.dockerignore   text eol=lf
*.yml           text eol=lf
*.yaml          text eol=lf
.env.example    text eol=lf
requirements*.txt text eol=lf

# --- Python: LF everywhere, so a file edited on Windows and read in a container
#     hashes the same either side ---
*.py            text eol=lf

# --- host-only scripts: Windows line endings are correct for these ---
*.ps1           text eol=crlf
*.bat           text eol=crlf
*.cmd           text eol=crlf

# --- binary, never touched ---
*.png           binary
*.parquet       binary
*.joblib        binary
*.zip           binary
*.pdf           binary
